<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak Q1 1997 C/A deficit rises to $478.7 mln.</title>
<headline>Slovak Q1 1997 C/A deficit rises to $478.7 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovakia's current account deficit rose to $478.7 million in the first quarter of 1997, versus $419.6 million in the same period in 1996, the Slovak National Bank (NBS) said on Friday.  </p>
<p>  SLOVAK CURRENT ACCOUNT     Q1 1997   Q1 1996    FY/96</p>
<p>  current account (in $million)  -478.7    -419.6   -1,940.8</p>
<p>  trade balance		  -477.2    -514.8   -2,105.8</p>
<p>  balance of services	   -19.1     +52.9	 +7.4</p>
<p>  income balance		  -14.8     +22.5	-44.7</p>
<p>  current transfers	     +32.5     +19.8     +202.3</p>
<p>-- Robin Shepherd, Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-521-8402</p>
</text>
